{
  "_comment": "ETP-6050 S2 — shared by the SPA (invoiceInboxReviewModel.test.js) and the backend (InvoiceInboxTotals JUnit). Formula: unit6 = round6(unitPrice*(1-discount/100)); net = round2(quantity*unit6); tax per rate = round2(sum(net)*rate/100); HALF_UP away from zero. Lines without taxRate add to the base only. Expected values are exact decimal STRINGS (unit6 with 6 decimals, money with 2). Rate rule (both sides): effective rate = the line's taxRate, else tax.rate of its resolved tax block; rounded HALF_UP to 2 decimals BEFORE grouping by rate and computing the tax; no rate at all = base only. Optional per case: `scale` (decimals of the document currency, default 2: money strings, nets, bases and amounts use it; unit6 stays 6). Optional per line: tax.docTaxAmount 'D' (default: tax once per rate on the sum of the nets) or 'L' (tax of each line rounded and summed). Expected taxes rows: one per (rate, mode), ascending by rate, D before L, with `docTaxAmount` when 'L'.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "no discount, one rate",
      "lines": [
        {
          "quantity": 2,
          "unitPrice": 10,
          "taxRate": 21
        }
      ],
      "expected": {
        "lines": [
          {
            "unit6": "10.000000",
            "net": "20.00"
          }
        ],
        "base": "20.00",
        "taxes": [
          {
            "rate": 21,
            "base": "20.00",
            "amount": "4.20"
          }
        ],
        "linesTotal": "24.20"
      }
    },
